## 🚀 Quick start

{% if ros2_pkg %}
The package ships an example node that publishes on the `chatter` topic:

```sh
# Terminal 1
ros2 run {{ repo_name }} {{ repo_name if pkg_language == 'python' else 'talker' }}
# Terminal 2
ros2 topic echo /chatter
```

Replace the sample node in `{{ package_name }}/main.py`{% if pkg_language == 'cpp' %} / `src/talker.cpp`{% endif %}
with your own ROS 2 logic.
{% elif micropython_pkg %}The firmware blinks the on-board LED. With a device connected:

```sh
{{ 'uv run --locked ' if package_manager == 'uv' else ('pixi run -e dev --locked ' if package_manager == 'pixi' else 'poetry run ') }}mpremote connect auto run firmware/main.py
```

The device-independent logic lives in `firmware/core/` (unit-tested under
CPython with `pytest`); board pins live in `firmware/board_config.py`; the
wire-up that MicroPython runs on boot is `firmware/main.py`. Replace the
sample blink with your own firmware logic.
{% else %}```python
from {{package_name}} import __version__

print(f"Hello {{package_name}} {__version__}")
```

Or if it is a commandline tool:

```sh
python -m {{package_name}} --version
```
